📘 DAX Measures Documentation
Zepto Sales & Inventory Analysis – Power BI
📌 Overview

This document explains all DAX measures used in the Zepto Sales & Inventory Dashboard.

The measures are designed to support:

Sales performance tracking

Inventory monitoring

Category & price analysis

Time-based trend evaluation

Business KPI reporting

📂 Data Model Tables (Assumed)
Table Name	Description
Sales	Transaction-level sales data
Date	Calendar table
Product	Item & category details
Inventory	Stock availability information
🧮 Core Sales Measures
🔹 Total Sales
Total Sales =
SUM ( Sales[Total Sales] )


📌 Purpose:
Calculates overall revenue generated.

🔹 Total MRP
Total MRP =
SUM ( Sales[MRP in Rs] )


📌 Used to compare actual selling price vs MRP.

🔹 Average Price
Average Price =
AVERAGE ( Sales[DiscountedSellingPrice] )


📌 Shows average selling price across all items.

🔹 Total Quantity Sold
Total Quantity =
SUM ( Sales[Quantity] )

📊 KPI Measures
🔹 Total Items
Total Items =
DISTINCTCOUNT ( Sales[ItemNameID] )

🔹 Total Categories
Total Categories =
DISTINCTCOUNT ( Sales[CategoryID] )

🔹 Total Orders
Total Orders =
COUNTROWS ( Sales )

📅 Time Intelligence Measures
🔹 Monthly Sales
Monthly Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    VALUES ( 'Date'[Month Name] )
)

🔹 Yearly Sales
Yearly Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    VALUES ( 'Date'[Year] )
)

🔹 Sales by Day Name
Day Wise Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    VALUES ( 'Date'[Day Name] )
)

📦 Inventory Measures
🔹 Healthy Stock Sales
Healthy Stock Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Stock Status] = "HEALTHY"
)

🔹 Low Stock Sales
Low Stock Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Stock Status] = "LOW STOCK"
)

🔹 Out of Stock Sales
Out of Stock Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Stock Status] = "OUT OF STOCK"
)

🔹 Stock Contribution %
Stock Contribution % =
DIVIDE (
    [Total Sales],
    CALCULATE ( [Total Sales], ALL ( Sales[Stock Status] ) )
)


📌 Used in donut and percentage visuals.

💰 Price Category Measures
🔹 Budget Sales
Budget Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Price_Category] = "Budget"
)

🔹 Mid-Range Sales
Mid Range Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Price_Category] = "Mid-Range"
)

🔹 Premium Sales
Premium Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    Sales[Price_Category] = "Premium"
)

🔹 Price Category Count
Price Category Count =
COUNT ( Sales[Price_Category] )

🏷 Category Analysis Measures
🔹 Category Sales
Category Sales =
CALCULATE (
    [Total Sales],
    VALUES ( Sales[Category] )
)

🔹 Top Category Rank
Category Rank =
RANKX (
    ALL ( Sales[Category] ),
    [Total Sales],
    ,
    DESC
)

🔹 Top 10 Categories Filter
Top 10 Category =
IF ( [Category Rank] <= 10, 1, 0 )


📌 Used as a visual-level filter.

📈 Performance Metrics
🔹 Sales % of Total
Sales % of Total =
DIVIDE (
    [Total Sales],
    CALCULATE ( [Total Sales], ALL ( Sales ) )
)

🔹 Average Sales per Item
Avg Sales per Item =
DIVIDE (
    [Total Sales],
    [Total Items]
)

📊 Dashboard Measures Mapping
Dashboard Visual	Measures Used
KPI Cards	Total Sales, Total Items, Categories, Avg Price
Monthly Trend	Monthly Sales
Day-wise Sales	Day Wise Sales
Stock Donut	Healthy / Low / Out of Stock Sales
Price Breakdown	Budget / Mid / Premium Sales
Top Categories	Category Sales + Rank
Tables	Total Sales, Quantity, MRP
